<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Urica</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venezuelan-war-of-independence">Venezuelan War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Urica was fought on 5 December 1814 in eastern Venezuela between royalist forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-tomas-boves">José Tomás Boves</a> and the last patriot army, led by José Félix Ribas. The royalists won, but Boves was killed by a lance during the fighting. The defeat ended the Second Republic of Venezuela, and Ribas was captured and executed soon afterwards.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Boves was killed at <b>Urica</b> in December 1814, but the republic had collapsed, and Bolívar withdrew to New Granada and in 1815 into exile in Jamaica.</blockquote><a href="/state/second-republic-of-venezuela">Second Republic of Venezuela</a></li></ul></section>
